{'symbol': 'CF', 'date': '2019-10-31 20:30:00', 'title': 'CF Industries Holdings Posts Q3 Earnings Per Share Of $0.29', 'text': 'CF INDUSTRIES HOLDINGS, INC. REPORTS NINE MONTH 2019 NET EARNINGS OF $438 MILLION, EBITDA OF $1,314 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.29.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.35 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.GROSS AMMONIA PRODUCTION FOR Q3 WAS MORE THAN 2.3 MILLION TONS.EXPECTS GROSS AMMONIA PRODUCTION DURING Q4 TO BE HIGHER THAN IN Q3.QTRLY NET SALES $1,038 MILLION VERSUS $1,040 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $1.06 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY SALES VOLUMES WERE SIMILAR TO PRIOR YEAR PERIODS.COMPANY EXPECTS THAT NITROGEN INDUSTRY FUNDAMENTALS WILL CONTINUE TO IMPROVE IN BOTH NEAR- AND LONGER-TERM.IN NEAR-TERM, DEMAND FROM IMPORT-DEPENDENT REGIONS SHOULD SUPPORT GLOBAL PRICING.COMPANY EXPECTS THAT GLOBAL DEMAND GROWTH FOR NITROGEN OVER NEXT FOUR YEARS WILL OUTPACE NET CAPACITY ADDITIONS.NET CHINESE-PRODUCED UREA EXPORTS ARE LIKELY TO BE IN A RANGE OF 1-3 MILLION METRIC TONS ANNUALLY.CAPITAL EXPENDITURES IN 2019 ARE PROJECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $425 MILLION.'}
{'symbol': 'CHTR', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': "Charter Communications to Launch AMC Networks' Full Suite of Streaming Services", 'text': "Charter Communications to Launch AMC Networks' Full Suite of - Streaming Services--Acorn TV, Shudder, Sundance Now and UMC--to - Spectrum Customers AMC Networks announced that Charter Communications, Inc. will launch its full suite of subscription video on demand services as well as AMC Premiere, the company's premium ad-free version of its AMC channel, to Charter's Spectrum customers. The launch of AMC Premiere, Acorn TV, Shudder, Sundance Now and UMC will bring Spectrum customers access to a wide variety of exclusive, diverse and AMC Networks content, including the Emmy-Award winning Killing Eve (AMC Premiere), Doc Martin (Acorn TV), Creepshow (Shudder), the Emmy Award-winning State of the Union (Sundance Now) and Craig Ross Jr.'s Monogamy (UMC). The services will be offered on the majority of Spectrum set-top boxes in the coming months. The launch is part of a recent broader long-term agreement between the two companies that includes continued carriage of AMC Networks' AMC, BBC AMERICA, IFC, SundanceTV, WE tv and BBC World News linear television networks as well as an extension of a previously announced co-production arrangement between the companies."}
