{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-10-31 13:30:00', 'title': 'Corteva Says Lack Of Rainfall Is Delaying Soybean Planting In Brazil - Conf Call', 'text': 'CORTEVA SAYS LACK OF RAINFALL IS DELAYING SOYBEAN PLANTING IN BRAZIL, WHICH MAY HAVE AN IMPACT ON SECOND CROP - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS EXPECT MORE NORMAL CONDITIONS TO ARRIVE IN MANY SECTORS OF THE AGRICULTURAL MARKETS IN 2020 - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS IN NORTH AMERICA, UNPRECEDENTED PLANTING SEASON HAS NOW GIVEN AWAY TO AN EXTRAORDINARILY LATE HARVEST - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS WE ARE RELATIVELY INSULATED FROM CURRENCY DEVALUATION IN ARGENTINA AS SALES ARE PREDOMINANTLY DONE IN U.S. DOLLARS - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS GOVERNMENT POLICIES UNFAVORABLE TO AGRICULTURE IN ARGENTINA, WOULD IMPACT OUTLOOK FOR 2020 AND BEYOND - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS REGULATORY DEVELOPMENTS IN EUROPE, BAN OF CORPORATES INSECTICIDE IN SEVERAL COUNTRIES, HAVE NOT HAD MEANINGFUL IMPACT ON QUARTER  - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS CURRENCY, PARTICULARLY DEVALUATION OF BRAZILIAN REAL, IS EXPECTED TO REDUCE H2 RESULTS BY ABOUT $80 MILLION OVERALL - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS EXPECT TO HAVE YEAR-OVER-YEAR IMPROVEMENT IN LATIN AMERICA - CONF CALL.'}
{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-10-31 09:30:00', 'title': 'Corteva Qtrly Operating Loss Per Share $0.39', 'text': 'CORTEVA - QTRLY GAAP LOSS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS $0.69; QTRLY OPERATING LOSS PER SHARE $0.39.CORTEVA - QTRLY NET SALES $1.9 BILLION, DOWN 2% WITH FLAT ORGANIC SALES.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-0.46, REVENUE VIEW $1.99 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.CORTEVA - SEES FY OPERATING EPS $1.20 TO $1.26; AFFIRMED FY GUIDANCE FOR NET SALES; SEES FY OPERATING EBITDA AT ABOUT $1.9 BILLION.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.17, REVENUE VIEW $13.86 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.CORTEVA - MERGER COST SYNERGIES REMAIN ON TRACK WITH FY COMMITMENT OF $350 MILLION.CORTEVA - RECENTLY AUTHORIZED INVESTMENT TO RAISE SPINOSYNS FERMENTATION CAPACITY BY 30%.CORTEVA - ADDITIONAL SPINOSYNS FERMENTATION CAPACITY WILL GENERATE MORE THAN $100 MILLION OF ANNUAL OPERATING EBITDA AT MATURITY.CORTEVA - QTRLY VOLUMES ROSE 3% AS DELAYED NORTH AMERICA PLANTING SHIFTED Q2 SALES INTO Q3; QTRLY LOCAL PRICE FELL 3%.CORTEVA - QTRLY CROP PROTECTION NET SALES OF $1.2 BILLION, DOWN FROM $1.4 BILLION.'}
{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'Corteva, Inc. Revises Earnings Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': 'Corteva, Inc. revised earnings guidance for the year 2019. The Company affirmed 2019 guidance for net sales. The Company revised its full-year operating EPS range, now expected to be between $1.20 and $1.26 per share. Using the mid-point, this represents a $0.04 improvement over the mid-point of the prior guidance.'}
