{'symbol': 'DD', 'date': '2019-10-31 13:30:00', 'title': 'Dupont Says Current Expectation Is That Semiconductor Market Recovery Will Continue - Conf Call', 'text': "DUPONT SAYS BELIEVE SOFTNESS WE SAW IN SEMICONDUCTOR TECHNOLOGIES IN Q2 DUE TO HIGH CHANNEL INVENTORIES IS RESOLVING - CONF CALL.DUPONT SAYS CURRENT EXPECTATION IS THAT SEMICONDUCTOR MARKET RECOVERY WILL CONTINUE, RETURNING TO GROWTH DURING 2020 - CONF CALL.DUPONT SAYS REMAIN CONFIDENT IN THE LONG-TERM GROWTH OF PROBIOTICS BUSINESS - CONF CALL.DUPONT SAYS  ANTICIPATE THAT REBALANCING OF NYLON 66 SUPPLY CHAIN WILL INFLUENCE PRICING IN VOLUMES AS WE LOOK TO REMAINDER OF YEAR - CONF CALL.DUPONT, ON TRANSPORTATION AND INDUSTRIAL BUSINESS, SAYS NOT SEEING A DEMAND PICKUP, BUT SEEING SOME SIGNS OF SOME SEQUENTIAL IMPROVEMENT - CONF CALL.DUPONT SAYS WE'RE LOOKING AT SIMILAR MACRO DYNAMICS FROM '19 INTO '20, GOING TO BE FAIRLY CAUTIOUS AS WE THINK ABOUT 2020 - CONF CALL.DUPONT SAYS TARIFF IMPACT IS NOT REAL HUGE FOR US, PORTION THAT'S DIRECT SALES TARIFF, IS ABOUT $50 MILLION ON FY BASIS  OF TARIFF IMPACT - CONF CALL."}
