{'symbol': 'WDC', 'date': '2019-10-31 20:30:00', 'title': 'Western Digital Announces CEO Succession Plan', 'text': "WESTERN DIGITAL ANNOUNCES CEO SUCCESSION PLAN.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - STEVE MILLIGAN INTENDS TO RETIRE AS WESTERN DIGITAL CEO; WILL CONTINUE TO SERVE AS CEO UNTIL A SUCCESSOR IS APPOINTED.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - BOARD COMMENCES SEARCH TO IDENTIFY COMPANY'S NEXT CEO.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - BOARD COMMENCES SEARCH TO IDENTIFY COMPANY'S NEXT CEO.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP -  STEVE MILLIGAN WILL CONTINUE TO SERVE AS CEO UNTIL A SUCCESSOR IS APPOINTED.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - ENGAGED HEIDRICK & STRUGGLES TO ASSIST IN CEO SEARCH PROCESS.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - BOARD WILL EVALUATE BOTH INTERNAL AND EXTERNAL CANDIDATES FOR NEXT CEO.WESTERN DIGITAL CORP - WILL EVALUATE BOTH INTERNAL AND EXTERNAL CANDIDATES FOR CEO."}
{'symbol': 'WU', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'The Western Union Company Affirms Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal 2019 and Three-Year Financial Targets', 'text': 'The Western Union Company affirmed earnings guidance for the fiscal 2019 and three-year financial targets. The company affirmed its full-year financial outlook, which was previously reported on August 1, 2019. The Company continues to expect the following outlook for 2019: Revenue GAAP: mid-single digit decrease; Adjusted constant currency: low single-digit increase, excluding any benefit related to Argentina inflation. GAAP EPS in a range of $2.47 to $2.57.The company affirmed the three-year financial targets announced September 24, 2019: Low double-digit EPS CAGR 2020-2022. Targets assume 2% to 3% revenue CAGR 2020-2022, no material change in major foreign currency rates, and no material mergers or acquisitions. The EPS CAGR is compared to 2019 adjusted EPS and assumes a mid-teens tax rate and $2.5 billion to $3 billion in anticipated share buyback and dividends over 2020-2022.'}
{'symbol': 'WMB', 'date': '2019-10-31 19:30:00', 'title': 'Williams Companies Posts Qtrly Adj EPS Of $0.26', 'text': 'WILLIAMS REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.QTRLY NET INCOME PER SHARE OF $0.18.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $1,999 MILLION VERSUS $2,303 MILLION.QTRLY ADJUSTED INCOME PER SHARE OF $0.26.QTRLY DISTRIBUTABLE CASH FLOW OF $822 MILLION - UP $58 MILLION OR 8%.REMAIN ON TRACK FOR 2019 GUIDANCE.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.25, REVENUE VIEW $2.08 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
{'symbol': 'WLTW', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'Willis Towers Watson Public Limited Company Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Willis Towers Watson Public Limited Company announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 1,989 million compared to USD 1,859 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 107 million compared to USD 17 million a year ago. Net income was USD 75 million compared to USD 44 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.58 compared to USD 0.34 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 0.58 compared to USD 0.33 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 6,349 million compared to USD 6,141 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 642 million compared to USD 339 million a year ago. Net income was USD 500 million compared to USD 317 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.86 compared to USD 2.4 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 3.84 compared to USD 2.39 a year ago.'}
